  "summary": "Wright Township supervisors voted to accept a donation from an anonymous local business of two Flock Safety ALPR cameras, which will be placed at undisclosed locations. There is no upfront cost to the township, but an annual fee of $6,000 begins in 2027. Chief Royce Engler cited neighboring Butler Township and Hazleton as successful users of the system.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Township supervisors at their December meeting voted to accept the donation of two Flock Safety cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "While there is no initial cost to the township, Engler said there will be an annual fee of $6,000 starting in 2027.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "As part of Flock Safety's system, police can request direct access to feeds from other law enforcement agencies as well as from privately owned Flock System license plate reader cameras in neighborhoods, schools and businesses.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
